                <pb facs="0811" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg723"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay transmits to Mr. McCormick the reply of the Japanese Government to the
                    proposal of the United States relating to the neutrality of China.)</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—See inclosure 2 to dispatch No. 45,
                    February 15, 1904, from Japan, printed on <ref target="#pg420">page
                    420</ref>.)</p>
            </div>
